b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:59:44-07:00","id":1107808,"title":"","content":"More books faster is always nice, but complaining that they aren't out yet isn't speeding the process up any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:01:58-07:00","id":1107810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1107805#post1107805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secrets of the Covenants was in development for two years. And complaining about the lack of previews tends to make Devs less motivated and less willing to post more previews or work on projects like the FAQ in their spare time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasnt complaining?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T01:20:06-07:00","id":1107938,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that a huge chunk of 1E content is very much relevant and still usable with a few tweaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T08:21:35-07:00","id":1108034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1107805#post1107805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secrets of the Covenants was in development for two years. And complaining about the lack of previews tends to make Devs less motivated and less willing to post more previews or work on projects like the FAQ in their spare time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Secrets of the Covenants example, among others, just proves this is not just an isolated issue with Signs of Sorcery or the MtAw line, it has been a systemic OPP problem. It benefits no one blaming individual Devs for the issue who probably have been overworked, distracted by having to wear too many different hats, and/or lacking sufficient resources but It is plain in the last few years OPP had a serious bottleneck and unbalance between ambitions and resources problem with several books getting seriously delayed or being apparently stuck in certain phases, such as development, for far too long. Say what you want, a project lacking apparent progress for 1-2 years is not business as usual even for RPG publishing, or at least it shouldn't be. No doubt in certain cases serious bouts of bad luck (see the infamous Wraith curse) and I suppose personal problems played a role too.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, from what has been told in Monday Meeting News, I understand OPP folk have recently acknowledged the issue and underwent some serious internal restructuring to try and ameliorate the situation. Some effects perhaps have been apparent already in somewhat increased progress speed for other books, sadly it seems MtAw is among the lines where this has been least noticeable so far. We can only hope there is going to be some catching up to speed down and across the line and the backlog is going to be cleared up for good. I wish very good things for all OPP folks for their efforts to keep so many gamelines alive, I'm quite grateful for the good quality of all the books that have managed to see the light of day in the end, and I'm happy for having been a patron to almost a dozen OPP kickstarters in the last few years. But I think it is unreasonable to pretend certain projects have not suffered severe problems in the past, or to expect fans are not going to be unhappy and impatient because of it (even if their remarks ruffle some feathers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 06-26-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T17:38:59-07:00","id":1108196,"title":"","content":"I understand its a small company working on many different things. However, its a hobby, and hobbies are fueled by interest. If there is nothing new to fuel the interest, the interest may wain and new hobbies be taken up. I am a LONG time Mage fan and I would be pretty bummed to have to lump Mage in with Exalted where interest went to frustration, then apathy and then just become forgotten. Onyx Path is doing wonderful things with games I loved as a kid, but it is starting to feel like they have to many irons in the fire that they can not focus on actually getting product out the door. I will have the $ ready to spend, yall let me know when you have the books for me to buy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/901-icarr757","name":"icarr757","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T17:43:04-07:00","id":1108198,"title":"","content":"The Dark Eras 2 Kickstarter is next Thursday, the 6th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T18:12:39-07:00","id":1108202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1108034#post1108034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Secrets of the Covenants example, among others, just proves this is not just an isolated issue with Signs of Sorcery or the MtAw line, it has been a systemic OPP problem. It benefits no one blaming individual Devs for the issue who probably have been overworked, distracted by having to wear too many different hats, and/or lacking sufficient resources but It is plain in the last few years OPP had a serious bottleneck and unbalance between ambitions and resources problem with several books getting seriously delayed or being apparently stuck in certain phases, such as development, for far too long. Say what you want, a project lacking apparent progress for 1-2 years is not business as usual even for RPG publishing, or at least it shouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, Onyx Path has published an astounding 11 full books and a good deal more supplementary material not in book form in the past 6 months. You gotta remember, OPP has a fuckload of properties they work on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T18:46:37-07:00","id":1108211,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the 2e core was good enough to keep me playing forever. I don't need new material to keep me interested in Mage. I'd love to see new material and it will keep me coming back for more, but at this point they could stop and I'd still be very happy. I know that's just my opinion, but really, isn't anything else just a bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T19:38:54-07:00","id":1108233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1108211#post1108211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the 2e core was good enough to keep me playing forever. I don't need new material to keep me interested in Mage. I'd love to see new material and it will keep me coming back for more, but at this point they could stop and I'd still be very happy. I know that's just my opinion, but really, isn't anything else just a bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div>As it concerns Signs of Sorcery specifically, my feelings at reading its content blurb released a year ago is this book is basically the second volume of the corebook (esp. as it concerns the Yantra and magical items parts) and its lack makes me perceive the 2e core as incomplete. I had more or less the same feeling about Mage20 before HDYDT and much more so Book of Secrets were released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 06-27-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:27:53-07:00","id":1108258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1108198#post1108198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark Eras 2 Kickstarter is next Thursday, the 6th.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note... with the Mage Dark Eras, there actually has been a significant amount of material released for Mage in the last year. Almost as much as the Free Council sourcebook. That's not insignificant, and it certainly puts to bed the notion that nothing has been produced for Mage lately. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1108233#post1108233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As it concerns Signs of Sorcery specifically, my feelings at reading its content blurb released a year ago is this book is basically the second volume of the corebook (esp. as it concerns the Yantra chapter) and its lack makes me perceive the 2e core as incomplete. I had more or less the same feeling about Mage20 before HDYDT and much more so Book of Secrets were released.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I have very different readings of the Core 2e then. Mage 2e strikes me not only as being complete, but as the most thorough and expansive corebooks of all of the 2e lines. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:56:55-07:00","id":1108309,"title":"","content":"How true is it that because Werewolf and Mage didnt get a kickstarter, the books have been slower because of it?<br /> <br /> Mage 2e is far from complete, explain the imbued item/artifact rules to me then. The fact so much gets discussed means that there has been alot of confusion etc. Any book (FAQ or signs) that helps shed light on stuff that was briefly mentioned in the core but could use with more extended text will help resolve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T03:50:27-07:00","id":1108335,"title":"","content":"Complete is not the same as perfect, and the rules will never be perfect. They are complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:32:15-07:00","id":1108389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage 2e is far from complete, explain the imbued item/artifact rules to me then. </div> </div> </div>Unclear != incomplete","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T16:41:09-07:00","id":1109022,"title":"","content":"I just wish OPP hired people to put out a reasonable number of books out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T16:50:12-07:00","id":1109027,"title":"","content":"Well, spread the word, get people buying things, posting their wants and requests. Can't justify increasing expenses if profits won't make up for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T03:28:42-07:00","id":1109169,"title":"","content":"OPP puts lots of books out in total but spread over their lines they release pretty slowly IMO. Very slowly in fact. I'd like to see more Mage stuff myself, been running my game for a while now and wanting Signs of Sorcery pretty bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T05:25:24-07:00","id":1109189,"title":"","content":"Much like other industries, OPP does what it can based on it's budget and manpower. The manpower is partially (mostly?) derived from its budget, which in turn is derived from its customer base. If OPP can't sell enough copies of books of any given game to justify focusing their effort on that game, then they won't focus on that game. That includes the incredible, amazing, astounding, addicting Mage the Awakening game.<br /> <br /> You want to see Mage books come out faster? Convince a hundred people that this game is worth buying the core rulebook (because it is). I want to see Mage books come out faster too, so I do my best to convince my friends that its a game worth playing. I've already managed to get three friends to buy, and we've already played several sessions together (so I know that they enjoy the game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T06:59:08-07:00","id":1109223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1109022#post1109022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wish OPP hired people to put out a reasonable number of books out.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, it's not as simple as &quot;just hire more people&quot;. Hiring people costs money, and if the books don't make enough money to cover that cost, the company goes under.<br /> <br /> Second of all, Onyx Path is publishing more than a book a month right now. Mage is only one out of over twenty games they produce. It has to wait its turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T07:03:33-07:00","id":1109225,"title":"","content":"Plus there's a learning curve involved in this stuff. If they did just hire people to write stuff and get it published as quickly as possible, you wouldn't likely be getting good stuff.<br /> <br /> That said, the call for writers is always open, if you or someone you know thinks they can write fast and well and wants to make money doing so then put it in an application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T19:52:38-07:00","id":1109558,"title":"","content":"Listen, if drive-thru RPGs award system is to be believed Mage The Awakening is one of the top selling games. In my opinion the main reason they concentrate on other properties like pugmire is because they own them and they aren't going to go down in a ball of flame like the rest of the world of Darkness becase of those new idiots running it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T20:24:29-07:00","id":1109571,"title":"","content":"There is also something to be said about oversaturating the market, and releasing unbalanced materials. If too many books are released, the game looks too big/ omex and more people won't invest in it than will. If books are released too quickly then they won't be balanced within the world they are set in. Imagine if Mages suddenly had an option that let them create Angels of their own, or if they could permanently replicate themselves, or even just make a sun in their hands at low level. Cool ideas, very unbalanced in the world of darkness. Alternatively, The options may be underpowered, resulting in there not being used. These things take time in order to be a viable but not making the base game worthless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T20:51:15-07:00","id":1109579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1109558#post1109558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listen, if drive-thru RPGs award system is to be believed Mage The Awakening is one of the top selling games. In my opinion the main reason they concentrate on other properties like pugmire is because they own them and they aren't going to go down in a ball of flame like the rest of the world of Darkness becase of those new idiots running it now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they're not concentrating on Pugmire any more than others. Dark Eras 2 is Kickstarting next week, half a dozen World and Chronicles of Darkness fiction books just got put up on Amazon.<br /> <br /> DriveThruRPG is just one site. Being a top selling game there is good, but it's not comparable to Steam or Amazon. These games live and die on world of mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:28:55-07:00","id":1109791,"title":"","content":"Guys. Seriously, 1 book since 2012. We're FAR from over saturating the market. LOL. You guys are hilarious.<br /> <br /> Obviously Dark Eras 2 is a good business idea, since it's useful to tons of lines, so no arguments there, but 1 book every 5 years is laughably bad.<br /> <br /> Certainly not Dave's fault, but it's terrible support on OPP's part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T09:41:06-07:00","id":1109799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1109791#post1109791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys. Seriously, 1 book since 2012. We're FAR from over saturating the market. LOL. You guys are hilarious.<br /> <br /> Obviously Dark Eras 2 is a good business idea, since it's useful to tons of lines, so no arguments there, but 1 book every 5 years is laughably bad.<br /> <br /> Certainly not Dave's fault, but it's terrible support on OPP's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark. Eras. There's about the same amount of Mage content between the two of them as three or four of Paizo's companion books. That's a hell of a lot more content than Pazio gives to any one class or race in the same period of time. <br /> <br /> If you want more support, that's fine, but it hasn't been one book in five years. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists