:[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T10:58:06-07:00","id":1109838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1109814#post1109814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On what grounds do <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/208162/Dark-Eras-To-the-Strongest-Mage-the-Awakening?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/202272/Dark-Eras-The-Sundered-World-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-Mage-the-Awakening?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> not count as books produced for Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are optional settings, you can take or leave them. Not having them wont matter, this shouldnt be the case with something specifically made to expand the 2e mage line. Also the fact they dark blue in colour means they produced for the chronicles of darkness line, we want nice mage coloured books please..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T11:11:33-07:00","id":1109844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1109838#post1109838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are optional settings, you can take or leave them. Not having them wont matter, this shouldnt be the case with something specifically made to expand the 2e mage line. Also the fact they dark blue in colour means they produced for the chronicles of darkness line, we want nice mage coloured books please..</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Colour? That's completely pedantic. If you're saying they don't count as books because they expand the setting, then I guess all five order books (2ell, six including the seers) and Tome of the Watchtowers are superfluous too. Actually, you could probably argue you could take or leave all supplements if you ran with that argument long enough. <br /> <br /> Look, if you want books that are primarily mechanics as opposed to settings, I get that and understand that. My point is that saying there has been one book in five years is willfully ignoring the stuff that has been created in the meanwhile. If it's not for you and you want a different type of book, that's a fine argument to make. Saying that nothing has been produced just because the stuff that has been produced isn't for you is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T12:13:30-07:00","id":1109859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1109791#post1109791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys. Seriously, 1 book since 2012. We're FAR from over saturating the market. LOL. You guys are hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one said Onyx Path was. The market is full of imitators, and it's a niche market to begin with. The need to get word out is even more important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously Dark Eras 2 is a good business idea, since it's useful to tons of lines, so no arguments there, but 1 book every 5 years is laughably bad.<br /> <br /> Certainly not Dave's fault, but it's terrible support on OPP's part. </div> </div> </div>You don't seem to understand how new editions or publishing work, but your complaints have been noted and I'm sure they're being given the consideration they're worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T12:45:24-07:00","id":1109871,"title":"","content":"LOL at a few Dark Eras chapters counting as reasonable support. It's meager. VERY meager.<br /> <br /> nofather, please don't claim I don't understand publishing just because I disagree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T12:51:30-07:00","id":1109875,"title":"","content":"The whining isn't and won't speed anything up, but it has been giving me a chance to indulge in some schadenfreude so please continue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:23:10-07:00","id":1109899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1109791#post1109791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys. Seriously, 1 book since 2012. We're FAR from over saturating the market. LOL. You guys are hilarious.<br /> <br /> Obviously Dark Eras 2 is a good business idea, since it's useful to tons of lines, so no arguments there, but 1 book every 5 years is laughably bad.<br /> <br /> Certainly not Dave's fault, but it's terrible support on OPP's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Johnny. Seriously. 11 books since January. We're FAR from a publishing drought. LOL. You are hilarious.<br /> <br /> Obviously Mage: the Awakening is a popular game line, since it's enjoyed by tons of players, so no arguments there, but putting other lines on hold so Mage can get more frequent support than any other Onyx Path product would be laughably bad.<br /> <br /> Certainly not ideal on Mage fans' parts, but it's excellent work on OPP's part getting so much out so fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:11:03-07:00","id":1110001,"title":"","content":"First and second drafts are done so the book is largely already written, it's just doing whatever it is that happens in development. <br /> <br /> I know parts of Changeling went thru rewrites during development, but I don't know if that is normal for development or not. <br /> <br /> I don't know what else goes into development honestly, wish I did. <br /> <br /> Still if some people are happy with the speed, and it's been along time, they have every right to complain and voice feedback as long as they are respectful. <br /> <br /> I have no doubt that there are many people who feel the same and it's a problem for some people, it will likely cost Onyx Path customers (not me, if I lacked patience, I'd already be gone) and you can tell Onyx Path knows that from some of the Monday notes in the past, I have a it's something they are working on. <br /> <br /> And for people interested in Mage, the release of none mage products has no bearing on them or there interests, so really changes nothing. <br /> <br /> Again, not in a rush, I'm pledging for the Pathfinder Kingsmaker video kickstarter game (still going) and will likely preorder Xathanar's Guide to Everything, so really in no rush if you get my drift. <br /> <br /> Just pointing out that some impatience is absolutely understandable at this point, and shouldn't be shrugged off, as long as it's expressed respectfully which it has been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T20:04:26-07:00","id":1110024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1110001#post1110001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And for people interested in Mage, the release of none mage products has no bearing on them or there interests, so really changes nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter if you care about non-Mage releases or not. They are happening, and they use up Onyx Path's finite manpower. I don't care about non-Elder Scrolls Bethesda games, and yeah, I'm a little miffed they're still not even working on an Elder Scrolls 6. But I I don't go around complaining that Bethesda's development schedule is unacceptable because they're not making Elder Scrolls games fast enough. Because I recognize that there are other people who do enjoy Bethesda's other IPs, who would be left out in the cold if Bethesda prioritized Elder Scrolls ar the expense of those IPs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T21:29:04-07:00","id":1110054,"title":"","content":"In a way, waiting for a new Mage book is a form of charity to those who aren't waiting for Mage, but are waiting for other OPP products. My patience is paying dividends in making more people than just myself happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T15:39:03-07:00","id":1110677,"title":"","content":"It's fair to say that my desire for more Mage books isn't satisfied by the publication of other books for game lines I am not interested in.<br /> <br /> Arguably some might say that OPP is trying to support too many lines and not getting enough out for each of them when considered individually, despite publishing a lot of books in total. I might argue that myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T16:58:01-07:00","id":1110693,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not arguing whether they're taking the right approach or not, I can't control that. I can control my attitude about it though, and I prefer not to be a whiner. I got by with Mage 1e not being updated for a long time and got plenty of joy out of the game. I can keep doing that in 2e with just one book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T18:16:56-07:00","id":1110713,"title":"","content":"An important catch to remember is that most of OPP's fanbase is <i>not</i> only interested in, say, Mage, but tends to have interest across the multiple lines. If by providing materials for that sort of an audience edges out the very small number of fans who <i>only</i> care about any one given line, it's not much of a loss, comparatively.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying they don't care, but they've clearly got priorities and worrying about the odd duck is obviously lower than worrying about the not-odd ducks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-02-2017, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T20:51:05-07:00","id":1110746,"title":"","content":"If anything, it does kind of prove how you should broaden your interests and not be stuck with one gameline from the one company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T20:56:07-07:00","id":1110748,"title":"","content":"I'm finding the entire discussion an ironic microcosm of life as we know it. In that light, damn, they might be right, but it still won't change anything for the foreseeable future. Bright side? It's a complaint over a series of a work of fiction, there's better stuff to expend energy on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T21:00:39-07:00","id":1110750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1107184-over-a-year-and-no-new-books?p=1109808#post1109808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a Class. It's a game line. 1 book in 5 years. LOL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's the inordinate amount of acronyms but, the OP seems to wish to be fed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}